.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt TAR 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm tar
.Nd create, list and extract POSIX ustar archives
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl c|t|x
.Op Fl v
.Fl f Ar archive
.Op Ar paths ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads and writes the POSIX ustar format.
It supports regular files, directories, symbolic links, modes, uid/gid fields
(written as zero for a non-root process), modification times and nested paths.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c
Create an archive from the path operands.
Directories are stored recursively.
.It Fl t
List archive members.
.It Fl x
Extract archive members below the current directory.
.It Fl v
Verbose listing or extraction.
.It Fl f Ar archive
Archive file; this implementation does not use standard input/output for the archive.
.El
.Pp
The name field is 100 bytes and the ustar prefix field is 155 bytes.
A path that cannot be split into those fields is rejected rather than truncated.
Long-name/PAX extensions, compression
.Pq Fl z , Fl j , Fl J
and unsupported member types are explicit errors.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A malformed archive or unsafe path exits with status 1; a usage error exits with status 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ar 1 ,
.Xr uuencode 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD implements the ustar subset described above.
